in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @magic/contract
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction

# @magic/distinction — the Spencer-Brown adapter species. Bridges the
# @magic family with @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction (Spencer-
# Brown's mark-of-distinction) honestly via the adapter pattern, NOT
# the decorative inheritance Seam caught at tick 7-10 (constraint C3).
#
# Tick 15 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 11's consolidation
# dropped the decorative `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction`
# from contract.mirror and audit.mirror; this species lands the
# adapter that re-establishes the structural relationship honestly.
#
# CRQ for tick 15: how to re-establish Spencer-Brown structural
# discipline at @magic altitude WITHOUT the decorative inheritance
# Seam C3 caught?
#
# Answer: an adapter species. The adapter takes magic carriers and
# MAPS them to distinction carriers; the structural inheritance lives
# in the explicit map, not in an `in` clause that buys namespace
# ancestry without carrier flow. The substrate-pull-correct way to
# compose substrate disciplines across families.
#
# === The adapter pattern ===
#
# Distinction's cross operation has signature `cross(m: mark, s:
# distinction_space) -> distinction_space`. @magic/contract's bind
# has signature `bind(s: magic_surface, m: magic_mechanism, promise:
# magic_invariant) -> magic_contract`. Different types; different
# arities; different return shapes.
#
# The honest structural relationship: bind is ANALOGOUS to cross
# UNDER THE FOLLOWING MAPPING:
#
# - magic_surface          ↔ mark
# - magic_mechanism        ↔ distinction_space
# - magic_invariant        ↔ (the boundary the cross draws)
# - bind operation         ↔ cross operation
# - distinction_well_formed ↔ invariant_preserved
#
# This species declares those mappings explicitly. A consumer that
# wants Spencer-Brown's discipline at @magic altitude can route
# through this adapter; consumers that want @magic without the
# distinction discipline route around it. No decorative inheritance.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# Adds:
#
# - `surface_as_mark(s: magic_surface) -> mark`: lifts a @magic
#   surface to a Spencer-Brown mark. The substrate-pull-correct
#   adapter primitive.
# - `mechanism_as_distinction_space(m: magic_mechanism) ->
#   distinction_space`: lifts a @magic mechanism to a Spencer-Brown
#   distinction-space.
# - `bind_satisfies_distinction(c: magic_contract) -> verdict`: the
#   bilateral verdict predicate. The FIFTH non-decorative `requires`
#   clause in @magic AND the FIRST cross-shard adapter `requires`
#   (consumes distinction's `distinction_well_formed` predicate via
#   the mapping).
#
# === Why the adapter pattern matters for future substrate work ===
#
# This species demonstrates the substrate-pull-correct way to compose
# disciplines across families. Future adapters can follow the same
# shape:
#
# - @magic ↔ @kintsugi (via reveal's settle-shape composition)
# - @magic ↔ @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis (via @magic/audit's
#   self-production semantics)
# - @magic ↔ @uuid/spectral (via spectral identity at @magic altitude)
#
# Each adapter explicitly maps carriers and discharges predicates;
# none uses decorative `in` inheritance.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994
#                               (*Design Patterns*). The OO adapter
#                               pattern. @magic/distinction IS the
#                               substrate-altitude adapter.
#   functor adapter             Category theory's adapter: an explicit
#                               functor between two categories
#                               preserves the discipline of both
#                               without forcing inheritance. The
#                               canonical mathematical ancestor.
#   Spencer-Brown mark          Laws of Form, ch.1 (Spencer-Brown
#                               1969). The discipline this adapter
#                               threads into @magic.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognition-81-runtime-magic-canonical-
#               spec.md §7 (the C3 hedge Mara preserved);
#               docs/specs/cascade-recognition-76-through-80-
#               canonical-spec.md §6.5 (the honest hedging from
#               tick 11 that this species closes).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (adapter pattern + functor: the substrate
#                       had two ancestors for this discipline before
#                       this shard landed),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-
#                       test]] (Reed's own discipline; the adapter
#                       makes the structural relationship empirical
#                       via the explicit mapping, not assertional).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (family-root),
#                 magic/contract.mirror (consumer of the
#                  bind_satisfies_distinction predicate),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction.mirror (the
#                  Spencer-Brown source the adapter threads).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/magic/distinction.mirror` declares `@magic/distinction`
# per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/cybernetics/spencer-brown-1969

prism @magic/distinction {
  focus distinction
  project distinction
  split distinction
  shift distinction
  settle distinction
}

# === surface_as_mark adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a @magic surface
# to a Spencer-Brown mark. The lifting IS the substrate-pull-correct
# way to apply distinction's discipline at @magic altitude.
#
# At Spencer-Brown altitude: the magician's gauge-visible interface
# IS the mark drawn at the @magic-altitude distinction-space; the
# audience-vs-trick partition IS the marked-state/unmarked-state.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
surface_as_mark(s: magic_surface) -> mark { \ }

# === mechanism_as_distinction_space adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a @magic mechanism
# to a Spencer-Brown distinction-space. The mechanism's matter IS
# the space within which the mark draws its boundary.
#
# At Spencer-Brown altitude: the mechanism's hidden content IS the
# distinction-space; the cross operation partitions it via the mark
# the surface presents.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
mechanism_as_distinction_space(m: magic_mechanism) -> distinction_space { \ }

# === bind_satisfies_distinction predicate ===
#
# THE FIFTH NON-DECORATIVE `requires` CLAUSE in @magic AND THE FIRST
# CROSS-SHARD ADAPTER `requires`. The bilateral verdict predicate
# discharging Spencer-Brown's discipline at @magic altitude via the
# explicit adapter mapping.
#
# requires distinction_well_formed(mark, distinction_space): the
# bilateral commitment that the lifted (mark, distinction-space) pair
# satisfies Spencer-Brown's well-formedness predicate (condensation +
# cancellation axioms; verdict partition).
#
# This is the substrate-pull-correct way to re-establish the
# Spencer-Brown discipline Reed dropped at tick 11 per Seam C3.
# The structural relationship lives in the explicit `requires`
# clause, not in a decorative `in` inheritance.
bind_satisfies_distinction(c: magic_contract) -> verdict
requires distinction_well_formed(surface_as_mark(c.surface), mechanism_as_distinction_space(c.mechanism))
{ \ }

out @magic/distinction
out surface_as_mark
out mechanism_as_distinction_space
out bind_satisfies_distinction
